# The step of an iterator of a list is laid out in line as arms that meet: it is finished or not, what it goes over is a view or a list, the position lies inside or not.
# In the typed copy of a loop an operation that may run other code begins the turn again in the closed copy: the arm in which it stands has left, and nothing has failed.
# The builder of the arms took itself for stopped from there on: the other arm and the blocks where the arms meet kept their edges and got no end, and the build stopped with
# "the walk is over and an edge leads to a block that has no end". The first such operation is the call that asks a view for its length.
